:question/id #uuid "4b477509-136c-5871-af67-2ab0b198668c" :question/math-academy-id "q-1952" :question/problem "Given that $y={2}^{9x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={2}^{u},\\,u=9x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={2}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{u} \\\\  & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{9x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1952/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1952"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection/21d9d9ed4ce616542edb555591f054a38ba8d1973844c96bc0f56fc9aaadb7da" :answer/id #uuid "7633ff09-2886-5821-8be3-cc8d80f2099d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "5bdc4471-b9b6-5880-8b98-6a56d357dddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection/d03d026bd09fec18424423a8366a5c537953c25f42714aa552e5fb2f8ee77fcb" :answer/id #uuid "39436a86-2e5d-5e32-bdcb-fd476c50c7e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection/36663a46a92af55c778e0bf95557a7900b042855b7ff6346c6de6ccdb29ade53" :answer/id #uuid "c9a276fd-4186-5034-8793-05c9b082fb70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection/74ee853a74bedf05b733a7c14956d27ed4f90878a7d2c31e17dc7391d99cd8a1" :answer/id #uuid "d18cb2a1-234f-5f46-a4c8-93978429738c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{{e}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26c38642-25c6-5f0e-b9b9-b362d2d7e047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107449/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-107449/selection/21d9d9ed4ce616542edb555591f054a38ba8d1973844c96bc0f56fc9aaadb7da" "q-107449/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-107449/selection/d03d026bd09fec18424423a8366a5c537953c25f42714aa552e5fb2f8ee77fcb" "q-107449/selection/36663a46a92af55c778e0bf95557a7900b042855b7ff6346c6de6ccdb29ade53" "q-107449/selection/74ee853a74bedf05b733a7c14956d27ed4f90878a7d2c31e17dc7391d99cd8a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107449" :question/id #uuid "77890d59-346a-5228-9be0-e4044f5213b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107449" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={e}^{3{x}^{2}-3}$ at the point where $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=3{x}^{2}-3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 6x \\\\  & =6x\\cdot {e}^{u} \\\\  & =6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=-1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & ={6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}-3}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =6(-1){e}^{3(-1)^{2}-3} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107449/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "107eaf98-be8c-5fb1-ac4c-948b1e00df0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-312451/field-1/6f0247031701f21c64b7d0257a7db3d64e7e3c14062668f001c79610c8b592f7" :answer/id #uuid "d471c6b5-2431-5ed8-b576-4e191ed19ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20x^4e^{4x^5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312451/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d9c6ce5-8de6-56dd-8bc7-59192c7a2d6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-312451/field-1/6f0247031701f21c64b7d0257a7db3d64e7e3c14062668f001c79610c8b592f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-312451/field-1/6f0247031701f21c64b7d0257a7db3d64e7e3c14062668f001c79610c8b592f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-312451" :question/id #uuid "6783757f-0379-51c5-a01c-1def6a588ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-312451" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={e}^{4{x}^{5}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=4{x}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (20{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =20{x}^{4}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =20{x}^{4}{e}^{4{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-312451/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "107eaf98-be8c-5fb1-ac4c-948b1e00df0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-312451"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
